  "id": "Compound::DB00420 - Gene::147",
  "verbalization": "Promazine is likely to interact with Adra1b through a shared molecular pathway involving Adra1d. The evidence suggests that Promazine binds to Adra1d, which then participates in adrenergic receptor activity, ultimately being participated by Adra1b. This implies a potential functional link between Promazine and Adra1b, where the drug's interaction with Adra1d may influence the activity of Adra1b. The varying specificity of the interactions—ranging from Alpha1-adrenergic to Alpha-adrenergic receptor activity—indicates that Adra1d may serve as a bridge between Promazine and Adra1b, highlighting a possible mechanism of action that involves receptor modulation. The integration of these pathways underscores the role of Adra1d as a critical mediator in the drug-target relationship, suggesting that Promazine may modulate Adra1b through this intermediate receptor.",
